SUMMARY:Hike & Swim the Grotto at Bruce Peninsula National Park
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/hike-swim-grotto)**\n\nWe'
 re doing a day trip to one of the most spectacular locations in Ontario: t
 he Bruce Peninsula National Park. This area is full of unique\, dramatic l
 andscapes with stark cliffs and views over the enormous Georgian Bay. We'l
 l be tackling a moderately difficult 8.5km hike through some of the most i
 ncredible summer scenery in Ontario.\n\nWe're starting the day off by visi
 ting the Grotto\, perhaps the most famous natural spot in the province. We
 'll hike through the forest then along the beach\, ending up at the incred
 ible rock formations and crystal clear waters of the Grotto. Here we'll st
 op for lunch\, taking in the incredible views and turquoise water before h
 iking on to the backcountry Stormhaven Campsite. On the way we'll cross pe
 bble beaches\, forest trails and unreal views of Lake Huron before coming 
 back the way we came.\n\n**Please note that self drivers will need to purc
 hase a permit for parking.**\n\n**Highlights**\n**Visit the Grotto:** Expl
 ore Ontario’s most famous natural landmark\, where striking limestone cl
 iffs meet crystal-clear turquoise waters.\n**Hike Pebble Beaches:** Walk a
 cross rugged shoreline beaches and forested trails that lead to the remote
  Stormhaven backcountry campsite.\n**Views of Georgian Bay:** Take in swee
 ping panoramas of cliffs and open water\, with autumn colours adding even 
 more drama to the landscape.\n\n**Event cost: $70+HST (for explorer member
 s) - $70 optional transport available.**\n**Register [here.](https://www.w
 ildernessunion.com/adventures/hike-swim-grotto)**\n\n**About Wilderness Un
 ion**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors community
  that connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps yo
 u find your people.\n\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The group is a 
 mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\
 n\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendance 
 - we typically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large enough th
 at there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not overwhelming
 !\n\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wi
 ldernessunion.com/)***
